.TH KINTSUGI-PROMPT 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-prompt \- inspect the compiled prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi prompt
show [\-\-text] [\-\-json]
.br
.B kintsugi prompt
diff
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect the compiled prompt manifest. The manifest shows what layers are
injected and their token counts.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP "\fBtest\fR"
Compile the prompt across every configured model and assert the invariants:
layer order, budget compliance, determinism, stack hash. \fB--model\fR for one
model, \fB--golden DIR\fR to write or diff manifests.

.IP \fBshow\fR
Compile and print the prompt manifest
.IP \fBdiff\fR
Diff this compile against the last one
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-text\fR
Print the compiled prompt itself
.IP \fB\-\-json\fR
Print the manifest as JSON
.SH EXAMPLES
View manifest:
.PP
  $ kintsugi prompt show
.PP
View the prompt text:
.PP
  $ kintsugi prompt show --text
.PP
Compare to last compile:
.PP
  $ kintsugi prompt diff
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1)
